### 2. Backend: Core Services & WebSocket Gateway

#### [NEW] [`backend/src/services/varka-context.service.ts`](file:///c:/github/varka/varka/backend/src/services/varka-context.service.ts)
- Maintain structured, live operational context per user session:
  - `user`: name, email, role.
  - `activeSection`: current tab (tracking, forecast, optimizer, jit, risk, agent, history).
  - `voyage`: current selected voyage (vessel name, IMO, route, cargo, departure, ETA, status, risk).
  - `tracking`: real-time speed, coordinates, heading, distance remaining, navigation alerts.
  - `prediction`: route ID, current rate, 60-day forecast outlook, confidence intervals (P10/P90), key drivers.
  - `marine`: wave height, wind, sea state, weather risk.
  - `vesselOptimization`: recommended class, DWT utilisation %, feasibility score.
  - `jit`: recommended speed, anchorage wait avoided, fuel saved, CO2 reduced.
  - `charterStrategy`: multi-voyage rates, discounts, expected savings.
  - `agentAnalysis`: quoted rate, landed cost min/max, hidden cost variance %.
  - `recentEvents`: chronological operational event log.
- Provide methods:
  - `initializeContext(userId, initialData)`
  - `updateContext(userId, path, value, source)`
  - `mergeContext(userId, partialContext)`
  - `getFormattedPromptContext(userId)`: produces a clean, concise markdown/JSON summary for the Gemini prompt without exceeding token limits.

#### [NEW] [`backend/src/services/gemini.service.ts`](file:///c:/github/varka/varka/backend/src/services/gemini.service.ts)
- Dedicated Gemini API integration with streaming support:
  - System prompt enforcing strict adherence to supplied Varka operational context.
  - Conversational memory management for active session.
  - Streams text chunks as they arrive from Gemini.
  - Grounded fallback generator if `GEMINI_API_KEY` is not set or rate limits occur.

#### [NEW] [`backend/src/websocket/varka-intelligence.gateway.ts`](file:///c:/github/varka/varka/backend/src/websocket/varka-intelligence.gateway.ts)
- Attaches to the Express HTTP server on route `/ws/varka-intelligence`.
- Handles WebSocket connection lifecycle:
  - **Authentication Handshake:** Extracts JWT from connection URL query parameter (`?token=...`), `Authorization` header, or cookie. Verifies using `jwtService.verifyAccessToken(token)`. Rejects unauthorized connections with code `4001`.
  - **Message Dispatcher:**
    - `chat.send`: Triggers context generation and calls `gemini.service.ts` with streaming tokens back to the client (`chat.start`, `chat.token`, `chat.complete`, `chat.error`).
    - `context.update` & `context.sync`: Updates the session's live operational context in real time.
    - `chat.history.clear`: Resets active session conversation.
  - **Heartbeat & Ping/Pong:** Detects stale sockets and manages clean reconnection.

#### [MODIFY] [`backend/src/server.ts`](file:///c:/github/varka/varka/backend/src/server.ts)
- Initialize and attach `VarkaIntelligenceGateway` to the HTTP server created by `app.listen()`.

